<title>MEXICO: Mexico reopens Dos Bocas crude port - Pemex.</title>
<headline>Mexico reopens Dos Bocas crude port - Pemex.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's crude oil shipping port Dos Bocas reopened Tuesday at 0640 local time (1240 GMT), a spokeswoman from the state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said.</p>
<p>The port, situated in the Gulf of Mexico in Tabasco state, was closed Saturday in the face of strong winds and waves of between 10 and 12 feet, port authority officials said.</p>
<p>Dos Bocas was the only port of the country's three main crude shipping terminals closed due to bad weather.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903.</p>
</text>
